# EvoMan Genetic Algorithm Fitness Comparison

This project investigates how the design of a fitness function influences
the evolution and performance of specialist agents in the
[EvoMan framework](https://github.com/karinemiras/evoman_framework).

Two Genetic Algorithms are compared while using the same evolutionary
operators and neural-network controller structure.

## Objective

The goal is to evolve specialist agents capable of defeating individual
EvoMan enemies and to evaluate how different fitness functions affect
their performance and convergence.

The experiments are performed separately against:

- Enemy 4
- Enemy 6
- Enemy 7

## Algorithms

### GA1

GA1 uses the default EvoMan fitness function.

It balances:

- reducing enemy energy
- preserving player energy
- minimizing fight duration

### GA2

GA2 uses a custom fitness function with a stronger linear time penalty:

```text
fitness = 100 - enemy_energy - 0.05 * time_alive
